    "notes": "1. 'Cash and cash equivalents' is composed of the two line items explicitly detailed in Note 32. 'Restricted cash' is excluded as it is not available for general use. 2. 'Marketable securities' includes current financial assets at FVPL and FVOCI, which are liquid, unrestricted investments intended for sale in the near term. For 2023, the FVOCI current asset was '–' (zero), so only FVPL is included. Non-current financial assets are not considered marketable as they are not held for short-term trading. 3. 'Total accounts receivable' is the net carrying amount from the balance sheet. 4. 'Total current liabilities' is the sum of all line items listed under 'Current liabilities' in the balance sheet. 5. 'Total debt short-term and long-term' includes all borrowings and notes payable from both current and non-current liabilities, aligning with the definition in the supplementary 'Total debts' table (Note 4.2). 6. 'Total equity' is the sum of equity attributable to equity holders and non-controlling interests. 7. All values are in RMB millions (scale: 1E6).",
